.TH MU2EDAQ-OTSDAQ 1 "2026-07-27" "mu2edaq-commandline-tools 0.2.0" "Mu2e DAQ"
.SH NAME
mu2edaq-tools otsdaq \- read status and diagnostics from a running otsdaq instance
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mu2edaq-tools otsdaq
.I read-command
.RI [ options ]
.PP
.B mu2edaq-tools otsdaq raw
.I RequestType
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The otsdaq command group is a synchronous Python client for the xdaq HTTP
endpoints observed in the Mu2e otsdaq packages. Modeled commands are
read-only. They print a terminal-oriented view by default and a stable JSON
envelope with
.BR --json .
.PP
The JSON envelope contains
.IR instance ,
.IR command ,
.IR timestamp ,
and
.IR data .
With
.BR --watch ,
one envelope is emitted per line (NDJSON).
.SH READ COMMANDS
.TP
.B state
Current run-control state.
.TP
.BI "run-info [" RUN_NUMBER ]
Current run information when omitted or zero, or information for the requested
run number.
.TP
.BR daq-report ", " daq-state
TFM/artdaq report and process state.
.TP
.B macros
Runtime FE, public, and private macro inventory. This does not execute a macro.
.TP
.BR pv-list ", " "pv-read " "PV..." ", " "pv-settings " "PV..."
List PVs or read values and settings through Slow Controls.
.TP
.BR "alarms [" "PV..." "]" ", " alarm-checks
Read alarm data or the dashboard alarm-check status.
.TP
.BI "console [" "--lcount N" ]
Read console messages. Watch mode carries the returned count into the next
request when the server supplies one.
.TP
.BI "messages [" --history ]
Read gateway system messages.
.SH COMMON OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "--instance " NAME
Select a named profile. Otherwise
.B otsdaq.default_instance
is required.
.TP
.BI "--gateway-url " ORIGIN
Override the Gateway, Console, and Macro Maker origin.
.TP
.BI "--slow-controls-url " ORIGIN
Override the Slow Controls origin. The default is the gateway port plus one.
.TP
.BI "--tfm-url " ORIGIN
Override the TFM origin. The default is the gateway host on port 3047.
.TP
.BI "--timeout " SECONDS
HTTP timeout. Default: 10 seconds.
.TP
.BR --verify-tls ", " --insecure
Enable or disable server certificate verification. The Phase 1 default is
insecure and emits a warning on stderr.
.TP
.BI "--ca-bundle " FILE
Use a custom CA bundle and enable verification.
.TP
.B --json
Emit a stable JSON envelope instead of the human view.
.TP
.B --watch
Poll until interrupted or until
.B --count
samples have been emitted.
.TP
.BI "--interval " SECONDS
Polling interval. Default: 2 seconds.
.TP
.BI "--count " N
Bound watch mode to N samples.
.SH RAW REQUESTS
.B raw
is an expert escape hatch and is not read-only. It can invoke configuration
writes, macro execution, or state transitions and therefore warns on every
invocation. It never repeats automatically.
.PP
Options are
.BR "--service gateway|console|config|slow-controls|tfm|macro" ,
.BI "--lid " N ,
.BR "--handler request|state-machine" ,
repeated
.BI "--query " KEY=VALUE
and
.BI "--form " KEY=VALUE ,
and
.B --xml
for the exact response instead of normalized JSON.
.SH AUTHENTICATION
Reads are anonymous unless a CookieCode is supplied through
.B MU2EDAQ_TOOLS_OTSDAQ_COOKIE
or a profile's
.B cookie_file .
Credential files must be owner-only on POSIX systems. Cookie values are never
accepted as dedicated command-line options or ordinary YAML values. The
credential is sent only to LID 281 (Configuration Supervisor).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Configuration, transport, HTTP, XML, embedded-JSON, or otsdaq response error.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid arguments.
.TP
.B 130
Watch mode interrupted with Ctrl-C.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
mu2edaq-tools otsdaq state --instance crv
mu2edaq-tools otsdaq pv-read Mu2e:TDAQ_crv:daq08DTC:Temperature --json
mu2edaq-tools otsdaq daq-state --watch --count 5 --json
mu2edaq-tools otsdaq raw getAppStatus --service gateway --xml
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mu2edaq-tools (1),
.BR mu2edaq_commandline_tools (3)
